<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">
        <p>Anyone can tag another Lively user in a livestream chat. Tagging refers to when you type the @@ symbol into a chat followed by the username of the person you want to tag (e.g., @@livelyuser).</p>
        <p>As you begin typing a username into chat, a list of usernames that match what you type will appear in a list that updates as you type.</p>

        <br><br><br>

        <p>If someone tags you in a livestream, you'll receive a push notification on your mobile device (depending on your notification settings).</p>
        <p>Note: Users are limited to how many times they can tag you in a given time frame. There are also limits to how many notifications you will receive when you are tagged multiple times in a livestream.</p>

        <h2>Viewing chats you were tagged in</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Open the Lively app on your mobile device.</li>
            <li>Tap the Notifications bell icon in the top menu. Notifications for chats you've been tagged in will appear with the following info:</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ul>
            <li>The username of the person who tagged you.</li>
            <li>The livestream in which you were tagged.</li>
            <li>The full message your username was tagged in.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>You can limit when you'd like to receive notifications when you're tagged by going to your <a href="#">notification settings.</a></p>

